{"availability":"available","full":"jingjing2222/react-native-nitro-geolocation","name":"react-native-nitro-geolocation","description":"A React Native Geolocation module Using Nitro","category":"Developer tools","language":"Kotlin","stars":115,"forks":8,"created":"2025-09-30T02:37:49Z","updated":"2026-09-13T10:59:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://react-native-nitro-geolocation.pages.dev/","topics":["android","fused-location","geocoding","geolocation","gps","ios","jsi","location","new-architecture","nitro","nitro-modules","react","react-native"],"demo":"https://react-native-nitro-geolocation.pages.dev/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:08.359Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:08.359Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:08.359Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:58:08.359Z","stars":115,"forks":8}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Nitro-powered geolocation for React Native apps","A native iOS/Android geolocation module for React Native 0.75+ apps using the New Architecture and Nitro Modules. Start by replacing @react-native-community/geolocation with /compat, then move to the typed API when you are ready. The current release line adds foreground web support through both the package import and /compat, plus a native Background Location API for tracking, geofencing, storage recovery, Headless JS, and HTTP sync.","In 2.0, Android foreground notifications accept custom actions: [{ id, title }]. Handle taps with onBackgroundEvent() or your Headless JS task using the notificationAction event and its notificationAction.actionId payload."],"features":["🎯 Simple functional API — Direct function calls, no complex abstractions","⚡ JSI-powered performance — Direct native calls without Bridge overhead","🔁 Compat API — Drop-in compatible with the core native community API","🧹 Automatic cleanup — No manual subscription management","📱 Consistent behavior across iOS and Android"],"